{"name":"Verona Beach","hex":"#e9d3ba","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"beach","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The shore of a body of water, especially when sandy or pebbly.","A horizontal strip of land, usually sandy, adjoining water."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To run aground on a beach.","To run (something) aground on a beach."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beach"}],"entries":[{"title":"Romeo + Juliet","blocks":[{"text":"William Shakespeare's Romeo & Juliet is a 1996 romantic crime film directed, produced, and co-written by Baz Luhrmann. It is a modernized adaptation of William Shakespeare's tragedy of the same name, albeit still using Shakespearean English. The film stars Leonardo DiCaprio and Claire Danes in the title roles of two teenagers who fall in love, despite their being members of feuding families. Brian Dennehy, John Leguizamo, Miriam Margolyes, Harold Perrineau, Pete Postlethwaite, Paul Sorvino and Diane Venora also star in supporting roles. It is the third major film version of the play, following adaptations by George Cukor in 1936 and by Franco Zeffirelli in 1968."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b4/William_shakespeares_romeo_and_juliet_movie_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Romeo_%2B_Juliet"},{"title":"Verona","blocks":[{"text":"Verona is the largest city in the region of Veneto in Italy, with a population of 255,139 as of 2026. It is one of the seven provincial capitals of the region, and is also the 2nd-largest city in northeast Italy. The metropolitan area of Verona covers an area of 1,426 km2 (550.58 sq mi) and has a population of 714,310 inhabitants. It is one of the main tourist destinations in Northern Italy because of its artistic heritage and several annual fairs and shows as well as the opera season in the Arena, an ancient Roman amphitheater."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Verona_cityscape_sunny.jpg/330px-Verona_cityscape_sunny.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Verona"},{"title":"Beach","blocks":[{"text":"A beach is a landform alongside a body of water which consists of loose particles. The particles composing a beach are typically made from rock, such as sand, gravel, shingle, pebbles, etc., or biological sources, such as mollusc shells or coralline algae. Sediments settle in different densities and structures, depending on the local wave action and weather, creating different textures, colors and gradients or layers of material."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Beach_at_Fort_Lauderdale.jpg/330px-Beach_at_Fort_Lauderdale.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beach"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Arche_scaligere_%28Verona%29.jpg/500px-Arche_scaligere_%28Verona%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Arche_scaligere_%28Verona%29.jpg/1280px-Arche_scaligere_%28Verona%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Arche_scaligere_%28Verona%29.jpg/500px-Arche_scaligere_%28Verona%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Arche Scaligere, tombs of the ancient lords of Verona","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AArche_scaligere_(Verona).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Leone_di_San_Marco_a_Verona.jpg/500px-Leone_di_San_Marco_a_Verona.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Leone_di_San_Marco_a_Verona.jpg/500px-Leone_di_San_Marco_a_Verona.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Lion of Saint Mark, located in Piazza delle Erbe, the symbol of the Venetian Republic","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALeone_di_San_Marco_a_Verona.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Palazzo_Barbieri-XE3F2501a.jpg/500px-Palazzo_Barbieri-XE3F2501a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Palazzo_Barbieri-XE3F2501a.jpg/1280px-Palazzo_Barbieri-XE3F2501a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Palazzo_Barbieri-XE3F2501a.jpg/500px-Palazzo_Barbieri-XE3F2501a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Palazzo Barbieri is Verona's city hall.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APalazzo_Barbieri-XE3F2501a.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/PanoramaCSP.jpg/500px-PanoramaCSP.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/PanoramaCSP.jpg/1280px-PanoramaCSP.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/PanoramaCSP.jpg/500px-PanoramaCSP.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A panoramic view of Verona from Castel San Pietro","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APanoramaCSP.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Italy_-_Verona_-_Arena.jpg/500px-Italy_-_Verona_-_Arena.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Italy_-_Verona_-_Arena.jpg/1280px-Italy_-_